---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '25 October 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — pi-homelab"
  description="Privacy policy for the pi-homelab site and the homelab-rclone Google API client."
>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt="" />pi-homelab</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p>
      This policy covers two things run by one person, aemreusta (“I”): this website, and
      <b>homelab-rclone</b>, a Google API client used by my own home server.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This is a static page served by GitHub Pages. It sets no cookies and runs no analytics,
      advertising or tracking scripts. GitHub, as the host, may keep standard server logs such as IP
      addresses; see the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What homelab-rclone is</h2>
    <p>
      homelab-rclone is a personal OAuth client for <a href="https://rclone.org/">rclone</a>, running on
      a server I own. It exists only so that this server can back up and archive its own files to my own
      Google Drive. It is not a product or a service, and it is not offered to anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2>What Google data it accesses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It accesses only the Google Drive of the account that authorized it, which is mine.</li>
      <li>It reads, writes and deletes files in that Drive in order to store backups and archived files, list them, and verify their checksums.</li>
      <li>It does not access Gmail, Contacts, Calendar or any other Google service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the data is used and stored</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Files are transferred directly between my server and my Google Drive.</li>
      <li>The OAuth token is stored only in the rclone configuration on my server, with access restricted to its owner.</li>
      <li>No data is sold, shared with third parties, used for advertising, or used to train AI or machine-learning models.</li>
      <li>No one other than me uses the client, so no other person's data is collected.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
    <p>
      homelab-rclone's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
      including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Revoking access</h2>
    <p>
      Access can be revoked at any time from the
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">third-party connections page of the Google Account</a>.
      Revoking it stops all access immediately; files already stored in Drive stay where they are.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Changes to this policy are published on this page with a new date. For questions, open an issue
      in the <a href="https://github.com/aemreusta/pi-homelab/issues">pi-homelab repository</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
